From: SoundTap contributors <soundtap@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] connect: ignore an empty track_uri/track_uid in skip_to

Picking a track in a list in the Spotify app sends an empty track_uri
next to the track_uid that identifies the track. 0.8.0 took the empty
uri, failed to resolve it ("Failed to resolve index by Some(Uri(""))")
and played the first track of the context instead. Treat empty values
as not provided, so the uid (or the index) picks the track.

Upstream: https://github.com/librespot-org/librespot/pull/1795 (merged
to dev, not in a release)
Signed-off-by: Stein Milder <info@steinmilder.nl>

---
 connect/src/model.rs | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/connect/src/model.rs b/connect/src/model.rs
--- a/connect/src/model.rs
+++ b/connect/src/model.rs
@@ -134,10 +134,11 @@ impl TryFrom<SkipTo> for PlayingTrack {
 
     fn try_from(value: SkipTo) -> Result<Self, Self::Error> {
         // order of checks is important, as the index can be 0, but still has an uid or uri provided,
-        // so we only use the index as last resort
-        if let Some(uri) = value.track_uri {
+        // so we only use the index as last resort. Clients may send an empty uri (or uid) next to
+        // the one that identifies the track, so empty values count as not provided.
+        if let Some(uri) = value.track_uri.filter(|uri| !uri.is_empty()) {
             Ok(PlayingTrack::Uri(uri))
-        } else if let Some(uid) = value.track_uid {
+        } else if let Some(uid) = value.track_uid.filter(|uid| !uid.is_empty()) {
             Ok(PlayingTrack::Uid(uid))
         } else if let Some(index) = value.track_index {
             Ok(PlayingTrack::Index(index))
